ent Disk Space\tUNKNOWN STEP\t2026-09-10T08:27:06.2592328Z scripts/ci/run-with-budget-warning.sh: line 156: /tmp/budget-status.mwvhb9/stdout: No such file or directory\n702:Measure Component Disk Space\tUNKNOWN STEP\t2026-09-10T08:27:06.2606006Z scripts/ci/run-with-budget-warning.sh: line 156: /tmp/budget-status.mwvhb9/stderr: No such file or directory\n1:# CI/CD Best Practices for AI-Driven Development (languages: en • [zh](CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.zh.md) • [hi](CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.hi.md) • [ru](CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.ru.md))\n5:## Why CI/CD Matters for AI Development\n16:## Recommended CI/CD Templates\n35:## Key CI/CD Principles\n42:### 1. Run Checks Only on Relevant File Changes\n99:#### Commit and ready-for-review checks\n117:#### Select monorepo suites from the workspace graph\n137:### 2. File Size Limits\n171:#### Adopt the limit with a ratchet\n177:### 3. Automated Code Formatting\n196:### 4. Static Analysis & Linting\n213:### 5. Fast-Fail Job Ordering\n239:#### Size jobs and start the longest work first\n245:### 6. Changeset-Based Versioning\n275:### 7. Validate the Actual Merge Result\n299:### 8. Pre-commit Hooks\n311:### 9. Release Automation\n334:### 10. Concurrency Control\n397:#### Preserve a full check when a commit arrives\n409:### 11. Secrets Detection\n417:### 12. Documentation Validation\n433:### 13. Container Images: Native Runners per Architecture\n469:### 14. Lint the Workflows Themselves\n489:### 15. Audit the Dependency Tree\n501:### 16. Prove You Can Publish Before You Build\n532:### 17. Tell a Broken Pipeline from a Changed World\n559:## Quality Enforcement Strategy\n579:## Getting Started\n588:### Add Swift CI to a multi-language repository\n595:## Automatic CI/CD Remediation\n611:### Why the issue is a Bug, and what it leaves out\n619:### Language → Template Mapping\n653:## References\ndocs/case-studies/**/*.log -diff\nscripts/ci/check-file-line-limits.sh:94:#   dev/log/                      issue evidence: other projects' logs and docs\nscript