r recovery to leave the report unresolved because GET returned 404.\n\n## Workaround and suggested fix\n\nFor a workflow already affected, bypass recovery for these URLs and re-run Lychee with its default GET behavior. In the recovery helper, use GET for ordinary URLs, bound each request and the whole retry pass, and discard the body after checking headers. Leave fragment URLs to Lychee unless recovery also validates the body and fragment. Keep a fixture with different GET and HEAD statuses so the gate cannot regress.\n\nLychee documents its default under [the request method option](https://lychee.cli.rs/guides/cli/#-x---method).\nEOF\ndir=dev/log/issues/135/pulls/136/upstream\nfor entry in '\"'js node scripts/recheck-broken-links.mjs' 'python python3 scripts/recheck_broken_links.py' 'php php scripts/recheck-broken-links.php'; do\n read -r lang interpreter script <<< \\\"\"'$entry\"\n repo=\"link-foundation/$lang-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template\"\n sha=$(cat \"dev/log/issues/135/pulls/136/github/$lang.ref\")\n cp /tmp/box-135-head-report.md \"$dir/$lang-head-get.md\"\n printf '\"'\\\\nReproduced at \"'`%s` with `COMMAND = [\"%s\", \"%s\"]`.'\"\\\\n' \\\"\"'$sha\" \"$interpreter\" \"$script\" >> \"$dir/$lang-head-get.md\"\n gh issue create --repo \"$repo\" --title '\"'Link recovery marks a GET 404 healthy when HEAD returns 200' --body-file \\\"\"'$dir/$lang-head-get.md\" >> \"$dir/reports.txt\"\ndone\ncat \"$dir/reports.txt\"'","aggregated_output":"https://github.com/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/322\nhttps://github.com/link-foundation/python-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/170\nhttps://github.com/link-foundation/php-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/41\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
