code changes\" detection:**\n92:**What always triggers checks when changed:**\n101:- **Commit tier (`synchronize`)** runs lint, type checking, and fast unit tests for changed packages, including on draft PRs. Aim for a 5–10 minute critical path.\n102:- **Ready tier (`ready_for_review`)** runs the heavy unit, integration, and end-to-end suites. Open the PR as a draft and mark it ready when the full check should start.\n139:**Enforce a maximum of 1000-1500 lines per code file.**\n160:**Synchronize the file-size ESLint rule with the CI check** to catch violations locally before CI:\n215:**Run fast checks before slow checks** to give the fastest possible feedback:\n249:- **Eliminates merge conflicts** - Each PR creates an independent changeset file\n250:- **Automates version bumps** - Highest bump type wins when merging\n251:- **Generates changelogs** - Release notes are compiled automatically\n252:- **Supports semantic versioning** - patch/minor/major bumps are explicit\n265:**Exempt docs-only PRs from changeset requirements:**\n277:**CI must test what will actually be merged, not a stale PR snapshot.**\n0\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
