[2026-11-27T06:57:52.860Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_130","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'p=dev/log/issues/135/pulls/136\nrepo=$(cat /tmp/box-135-templates-dir)\nPYTHONPATH=\"$repo/python/scripts\" python3 - <<'\"'PY' > \\\"\"'$p/verification/python-archive.log\"\nfrom unittest.mock import patch\nfrom check_web_archive import check_wayback_machine\nurl = \"https://example.com/deleted\"\nwith patch(\"check_web_archive.fetch_json\", side_effect=TimeoutError(\"mock Wayback outage\")):\n    unavailable = check_wayback_machine(url)\nwith patch(\"check_web_archive.fetch_json\", return_value={\"archived_snapshots\": {}}):\n    missing = check_wayback_machine(url)\nprint(unavailable, missing)\nassert unavailable == missing\nPY\nBOX_TEMPLATE_PHP=\"$repo/php\" php <<'\"'PHP' > \\\"\"'$p/verification/php-archive.log\"\n<?php\nrequire getenv('\"'BOX_TEMPLATE_PHP') . '/scripts/src/Http.php';\nrequire getenv('BOX_TEMPLATE_PHP') . '/scripts/src/WebArchive.php';\nuse LinkFoundation\\\\Template\\\\Pipeline\\\\{Http, WebArchive};\n\"'$url = '\"'https://example.com/deleted';\n\"'$lookup = static fn ($status, $body) => (new WebArchive(\n    new Http(static fn () => ['\"'status' => \"'$status, '\"'body' => \"'$body]),\n    static fn () => null,\n))->review([$url]);\n$outage = $lookup(503, '\"'Service unavailable');\n\"'$missing = $lookup(200, '\"'{\\\"archived_snapshots\\\":{}}');\nvar_export(\"'$outage);\nif ($outage !== $missing) {\n    exit(1);\n}\nPHP\ncat \"$p\"/verification/{python,php}-archive.log; gh issue view 54 -R link-foundation/python-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template --json title,body,state'","aggregated_output":"  Failed to check Wayback Machine for https://example.com/deleted: mock Wayback outage\nArchiveResult(available=False, archive_url=None, timestamp=None) ArchiveResult(available=False, archive_url=None, timestamp=None)\narray (\n  'archived' => \n  array (\n  ),\n  'missing' => \n  array (\n    0 => 'https://example.com/deleted',\n  ),\n){\"body\":\"## Problem\\n\\n`.github/workflows/links.yml` reports success when Lychee finds broken live links if every broken URL has a Wayback snapshot. The repository still contains and serves broken links; the Python helper only prints suggested replacements and does not rewrite them.\\n\\nCurrent terminal condition:\\n\\n```yaml\\nif: steps.lychee.outputs.exit_code != 0 && steps.webarchive.outputs.all_archived != 'true'\\n```\\n\\nThis makes an archived-but-not-replaced dead link a CI false negative.\\n\\n## Reproduction\\n\\n1. Put a known dead URL with an existing Wayback snapshot in a checked Markdown file.\\n2. Run the Broken Link Checker workflow.\\n3. Lychee returns a nonzero `exit_code`.\\n4. `scripts/check_web_archive.py` finds the snapshot and outputs `all_archived=true`.\\n5. The terminal failure step is skipped, so the workflow is green although the checked Markdown still points to the dead live URL.\\n\\nThe condition can also be reproduced without depending on a live site: feed the helper a fixture `lychee/out.md` containing `[404] <archived-url>`, observe `all_archived=true`, and evaluate the condition above.\\n\\n## Workaround\\n\\nFail on every nonzero Lychee result while retaining the Wayback step for actionable replacement diagnostics:\\n\\n```yaml\\n- name: Fail if broken links were found\\n  if: always() && steps.lychee.outputs.exit_code != 0\\n  run: |\\n    echo \\\"::error::Broken live links were detected.\\\"\\n    exit 1\\n```\\n\\n`always()` ensures the explanation runs even if the Wayback API/helper itself fails.\\n\\n## Suggested code fix\\n\\nChange the terminal condition as above and update its message to explain that an archive is a suggested replacement, not a reason to accept the still-broken source link. Add a workflow-structure test asserting the failure condition depends only on Lychee's nonzero exit and does not exempt `all_archived=true`.\\n\\nFound while auditing link-assistant/formal-ai#999 against template revision `bd07d1ce958cbc852a9ec9eae569f2064172b90f`.\\n\",\"state\":\"CLOSED\",\"title\":\"Broken link workflow passes when dead URLs have archives\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
