[2026-11-27T06:58:17.979Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_133","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'p=dev/log/issues/135/pulls/136\ncat > \"$p/upstream/python-archive.md\" <<'\"'EOF'\n## Problem\n\nA Wayback API outage is reported as an unavailable snapshot. At \"'`7a05d051`, the Python check returns the same result for a request exception and a valid empty `archived_snapshots` response. In both cases the CLI advises that it found no snapshot and tells authors to remove or replace the link. The broken link itself should still fail the check.\n\n## Offline reproduction\n\nRun from the template root with Python 3.11 or newer.\n\n```bash\nPYTHONPATH=scripts python3 - <<'\"'PY'\nfrom unittest.mock import patch\nfrom check_web_archive import check_wayback_machine\n\nurl = \\\"https://example.com/deleted\\\"\nwith patch(\\\"check_web_archive.fetch_json\\\", side_effect=TimeoutError(\\\"mock outage\\\")):\n    outage = check_wayback_machine(url)\nwith patch(\\\"check_web_archive.fetch_json\\\", return_value={\\\"archived_snapshots\\\": {}}):\n    missing = check_wayback_machine(url)\nprint(outage, missing)\nassert outage == missing\nPY\n\"'```\n\n## Workaround and code fix\n\nKeep Lychee'\"'s verdict and try a manual Wayback lookup after the API recovers before removing a historical reference. Make \"'`ArchiveResult` distinguish available, missing, and unknown. Give request failures and invalid responses the unknown verdict and emit a separate notice without asserting that there is no snapshot. Test a snapshot, an empty result, a timeout, and invalid JSON with mocks. Keep the broken-link failure in all four cases.\n\nFound in the audit for link-foundation/box#135. This concerns the recommendation printed by the archive helper. The workflow-level false success described in #54 is a separate issue.\nEOF\ncat > \"$p/upstream/php-archive.md\" <<'\"'EOF'\n## Problem\n\nA Wayback API outage is reported as a missing snapshot. At \"'`e12a25d7`, `WebArchive::snapshot` returns `null` after either multiple unavailable responses or successful responses with an empty snapshot collection. `WebArchive::review` then puts both in `missing`, so the workflow presents the outage as absence of an archive.\n\n## Offline reproduction\n\nRun from the template root.\n\n```bash\nphp <<'\"'PHP'\n<?php\nrequire 'scripts/src/Http.php';\nrequire 'scripts/src/WebArchive.php';\nuse LinkFoundation\\\\Template\\\\Pipeline\\\\{Http, WebArchive};\n\n\"'$url = '\"'https://example.com/deleted';\n\"'$lookup = static fn ($status, $body) => (new WebArchive(\n    new Http(static fn () => ['\"'status' => \"'$status, '\"'body' => \"'$body]),\n    static fn () => null,\n))->review([$url]);\n$outage = $lookup(503, '\"'Service unavailable');\n\"'$missing = $lookup(200, '\"'{\\\"archived_snapshots\\\":{}}');\nvar_export([\"'$outage, $missing]);\nexit($outage === $missing ? 0 : 1);\nPHP\n```\n\n## Workaround and code fix\n\nKeep Lychee'\"'s verdict and repeat the archive lookup manually after service recovery before discarding a historical reference. Retain bounded retries. Return a result that distinguishes a usable snapshot, a valid empty 200 response, and an unknown outcome when the API gives no valid answer. Add an unknown group to the CLI and describe it separately from missing archives. Use the injected fetcher and sleeper to test a 503 sequence, invalid JSON, a valid empty response, and recovery after an initial request failure.\n\nFound in the audit for link-foundation/box#135.\nEOF\nfor lang in python php; do\n  gh issue create -R \\\"link-foundation/\"'$lang-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template\" --title \"Wayback API outages are reported as missing snapshots\" --body-file \"$p/upstream/$lang-archive.md\" >> \"$p/upstream/reports.txt\" || exit\ndone\ncat \"$p/upstream/reports.txt\"'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
