[2026-11-27T07:02:09.157Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_161","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"p=dev/log/issues/135/pulls/136; rg -n -A37 '\"'^### 15'\"\\\\.' \\\"\"'$p/github/hive-mind-best-practices.md\"; cat \"$p/verification/\"{box-baseline-head-get,box-head-get,test-issue135-link-verdicts}.log; git check-ignore .playwright-mcp/; jq -r '\"'.[].artifacts[]|select(.expired==false)|[.id,.name]|@tsv' \\\"\"'$p\"/artifact-metadata/*.json; gh pr checks 136 -R link-foundation/box'","aggregated_output":"489:### 15. Audit the Dependency Tree\n490-\n491-**Code scanning does not audit your dependencies, and PR-scoped dependency review does not audit the ones you already have.** These two jobs look like coverage together and leave a hole between them: CodeQL analyses your source, while `dependency-review-action` runs only on `pull_request` and only inspects the dependencies a PR _changes_. An advisory published against a package that has been pinned for a year is invisible to both, forever, because no PR touches that line.\n492-\n493-```yaml\n494-- run: npm audit --package-lock-only --audit-level=high\n495-```\n496-\n497-- **Audit the lockfile as committed** (`--package-lock-only`). It reports what a consumer would get, and cannot be turned green by a resolution that only happens on this runner.\n498-- **Put the job on the schedule**, not only on push. A scheduled run is the only thing that can notice an advisory published after the code stopped changing.\n499-- **Set the level explicitly.** The default is `low`, which trains everyone to ignore the job; no flag at all is a different failure from a deliberate `--audit-level=high`.\n500-\n501-### 16. Prove You Can Publish Before You Build\n502-\n503-**A pull request exists to test the code; a push to the default branch exists to produce a release.** Those are different jobs, and a missing credential means different things to each. On a pull request it is a warning — forks have no secrets, and the code can still be tested. On the default branch it is the answer: if any credential needed for any planned release is unusable, nothing the run does afterwards can produce a release, and every minute spent building is waste.\n504-\n505-Put a `preflight` job first and make every publishing job `needs:` it.\n506-\n507-```yaml\n508-release-preflight:\n509-  runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n510-  permissions:\n511-    contents: read\n512-    id-token: wri… it\n513-  steps:\n514-    - uses: actions/checkout@v7\n515-    - env:\n516-        PREFLIGHT_MODE: ${{ github.event_name == 'push' && github.ref == 'refs/heads/main' && 'release' || 'report' }}\n517-      run: node scripts/preflight-credentials.mjs --mode \"$PREFLIGHT_MODE\"\n518-\n519-release:\n520-  needs: [release-preflight]\n521-  if: ${{ !cancelled() && needs.release-preflight.result == 'success' }}\n522-```\n523-\n524-- **Probe with a write, not with a login.** ghcr.io's token endpoint returns 200 for any scope and verifies nothing — the push then fails 403. docker.io answers an anonymous push-scope request with 200 and a pull-only `access` claim. Open a blob upload session (`POST /v2/<repo>/blobs/uploads/`) and cancel it with `DELETE <Location>`: one round trip, nothing stored, and the only form of the check that is not a guess.\n525-- **Report every failure, not the first.** The preflight's value is one report naming all missing credentials. A login step that aborts the job hides the rest, so make it `continue-on-error: true` and let the preflight script decide.\n526-- **Check reachability, not just writability.** A GHCR package is private on first push and stays private until someone clicks; publishing more versions of a package nobody can pull is exactly the compute this job exists to skip. GitHub exposes no API for package visibility (the packages REST API is GET/DELETE/restore only), so this is a manual step that the pipeline can only detect and name.\nRe-check: 1 lychee failure(s); 0 final, 1 eligible for retry\n::notice title=Link recovered on re-check::http://127.0.0.1:46803/missing failed temporarily in lychee but answers 100..=103,200..=299 now - not a broken link\nRe-check finished: 1 recovered, 0 still broken\nall_recovered=true: every failure in the report was retryable, and all URLs return an accepted status now.\nFAIL: HEAD 200 concealed GET 404\nBaseline exit 1 (expected 1)\nRe-check: 1 lychee failure(s); 0 final, 1 eligible for retry\nStill broken: http://127.0.0.1:37107/missing - answered 404, which lychee does not accept\nRe-check finished: 0 recovered, 1 still broken\nPASS: GET 404 kept the report unresolved\n✔ both consumers read errors and timeouts and ignore redirects (4.694886ms)\n✔ a runtime failure or incomplete report cannot be recovered (631.083777ms)\n✔ link recovery tests the same GET method as the checker (58.822749ms)\n✔ an archive outage or invalid payload is distinct from a successful empty lookup (6.671422ms)\nℹ tests 4\nℹ suites 0\nℹ pass 4\nℹ fail 0\nℹ cancelled 0\nℹ skipped 0\nℹ todo 0\nℹ duration_ms 716.478876\n.playwright-mcp/\n11932975000\tlink-foundation~box~XZRMEH.dockerbuild\n11932550239\tlink-foundation~box~KU4417.dockerbuild\n11932477928\tlink-foundation~box~AUURLQ.dockerbuild\n11932375406\tlink-foundation~box~AB9TA1.dockerbuild\n11932145311\tlink-foundation~box~J8YG80.dockerbuild\n11932136279\tlink-foundation~box~BULRGH.dockerbuild\n11932116105\tlink-foundation~box~MAN6B1.dockerbuild\n11932085397\tlink-foundation~box~IRTNLK.dockerbuild\n11931985768\tlink-foundation~box~H90Q1X.dockerbuild\n11931847160\tlink-foundation~box~12E1OD.dockerbuild\n11931841949\tlink-foundation~box~IU57L8.dockerbuild\n11931822389\tlink-foundation~box~IXQCIX.dockerbuild\n11931821619\tlink-foundation~box~I83TAB.dockerbuild\n11931736797\tlink-foundation~box~55AQXU.dockerbuild\n11931597675\tlink-foundation~box~WEQPFM.dockerbuild\n11931582940\tlink-foundation~box~Z1HAU5.dockerbuild\n11931572864\tlink-foundation~box~TZPJE0.dockerbuild\n11931519271\tlin