[2026-11-27T07:17:13.717Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_301","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '735,790p;819,857p' scripts/measure-disk-space.sh && sed -n '1,115p' dev/log/issues/135/pulls/136/README.md && tail -32 dev/log/issues/135/pulls/136/templates.md && ls -la dev/log/issues/135/pulls/136/verification\"","aggregated_output":"export SDKMAN_DIR=\"$HOME/.sdkman\"\nset +u\n[ -s \"$SDKMAN_DIR/bin/sdkman-init.sh\" ] && source \"$SDKMAN_DIR/bin/sdkman-init.sh\"\nset -u\n\n# --- Kotlin ---\ninstall_kotlin() {\n  set +u\n  sdk install kotlin < /dev/null || true\n  set -u\n}\nmeasure_install \"Kotlin (via SDKMAN)\" \"Runtime\" install_kotlin\n\n# --- Lean ---\ninstall_lean() {\n  curl https://elan.lean-lang.org/elan-init.sh -sSf | sh -s -- -y --default-toolchain stable\n  [ -f \"$HOME/.elan/env\" ] && \\. \"$HOME/.elan/env\"\n}\nmeasure_install \"Lean (via elan)\" \"Runtime\" install_lean\n\n# Load Lean\n[ -f \"$HOME/.elan/env\" ] && \\. \"$HOME/.elan/env\"\n\n# --- Opam + Rocq ---\ninstall_opam_rocq() {\n  sudo apt-get install -y bubblewrap 2>/dev/null || true\n  bash -c \"sh <(curl -fsSL https://opam.ocaml.org/install.sh) --no-backup\" <<< \"y\" || sudo apt-get install -y opam || true\n\n  if command -v opam &>/dev/null; then\n    opam init --disable-sandboxing --auto-setup -y || true\n    eval \"$(opam env --switch=default 2>/dev/null)\" || true\n    opam repo add rocq-released https://rocq-prover.org/opam/released 2>/dev/null || true\n    opam update 2>/dev/null || true\n    # Keep compiler failures visible and bound parallel builds on CI runners.\n    local OPAMJOBS=\"${OPAMJOBS:-2}\"\n    export OPAMJOBS\n    if ! opam pin add rocq-prover --yes && ! opam install rocq-prover -y && ! opam install coq -y; then\n      log_info \"Trying Ubuntu's Coq package after the opam build failed\"\n      maybe_sudo apt-get install -y coq || return\n    fi\n    if command_exists rocq; then\n      rocq -v\n    else\n      coqc --version\n    fi\n  else\n    return 1\n  fi\n}\nmeasure_install \"Opam + Rocq/Coq\" \"Runtime\" install_opam_rocq\n\n# --- Homebrew ---\ninstall_homebrew() {\n  local installer\n  installer=\"$(curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Homebrew/install/HEAD/install.sh)\" || return\n  PATH=\"/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/bin:$HOME/.linuxbrew/bin:$PATH\" NONINTERACTIVE=1 /bin/bash -c \"$installer\" || return\n  log_warning \"Installation of Homebrew failed\"\n  add_measurement \"Homebrew\" \"Package Manager\" 0 0\n  measurement_failed=1\nfi\n\n# Load Homebrew\nif [[ -x /home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/bin/brew ]]; then\n  eval \"$(/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/bin/brew shellenv)\"\nelif [[ -x \"$HOME/.linuxbrew/bin/brew\" ]]; then\n  eval \"$(\"$HOME/.linuxbrew/bin/brew\" shellenv)\"\nfi\n\n# --- PHP ---\ninstall_php() {\n  if command -v brew &>/dev/null; then\n    export HOMEBREW_NO_ANALYTICS=1\n    export HOMEBREW_NO_AUTO_UPDATE=1\n    brew install php || return\n    # `brew link` prints its \"Warning:\" lines on a *successful* link, so the\n    # output was filtered - but `| grep -v \"Warning\" || true` made grep's status\n    # the pipeline's and then discarded it, so a link that failed was\n    # indistinguishable from one that worked. The filter belongs on the output;\n    # the status belongs to brew. Anchoring the pattern also stops a line that\n    # merely mentions a warning from being deleted with them. (issue #123)\n    local brew_link_out=\"\" brew_link_status=0\n    brew_link_out=\"$(brew link --overwrite --force php 2>&1)\" || brew_link_status=$?\n    if [ \"$brew_link_status\" -eq 0 ]; then\n      printf '%s\\n' \"$brew_link_out\" | grep -v '^Warning' || true\n    else\n      printf '%s\\n' \"$brew_link_out\"\n      log_warning \"brew link --overwrite --force php failed (exit $brew_link_status)\"\n      return \"$brew_link_status\"\n    fi\n    \"$(brew --prefix php)/bin/php\" --version\n  else\n    return 1\n  fi\n}\nmeasure_install \"PHP (via Homebrew)\" \"Runtime\" install_php\n# CI/CD audit for issue 135 and PR 136\n\nThe audit covers the nine runs named in [issue 135](https://github.com/link-foundation/box/issues/135), their job and artifact metadata, the surrounding default-branch history, the [PR discussion](https://github.com/link-foundation/box/pull/136), and all four requested reference trees. The initial issue comments, PR conversation, inline reviews, submitted reviews, and required sub-issues were empty. The snapshots and inventories are in [github](github/).\n\n## Requirements and verification\n\n| Requirement | Finding and implementation | Verification |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Restore Links on main | The GitHub project formerly cited in the issue 80 case study returned 404 in two consecutive weekly scans. The case study now links to the specific Wayback snapshot identified by both runs. | Run 45443984715 lines 304, 336, 355 and 395, run 44115877567, and the GitHub API 404 in [verification](verification/). The archive replay from the local network was rate-limited. The snapshot URL came from two Actions lookups, and the availability API independently returned it with `available: true` and capture status 200. |\n| Fix false link verdicts across the pipeline | Retry completed, fully accounted-for scans only. Restrict rechecks to transient failures. Match the scanner's GET method and accepted statuses, preserve final failures for an otherwise recoverable URL, and leave anchor and local file validation to the scanner. Distinguish a failed scanner from a scan with broken links. | `test-issue135-link-verdicts.sh`, `test-issue121-links-recheck.sh`, and `test-issue131-links-recheck.sh`. The bounded localhost experiment gives HEAD 200 and GET 404: Box's baseline passes falsely and the fixed Box rejects recovery. |\n| Make archive diagnostics truthful | Both helpers parse the report's Errors and Timeouts sections; ignore successful redirects and the runner footer and preserve exact URL punctuation. Separate a valid response with no snapshot from a timeout, error status, or malformed payload. Bound requests and retain the original link verdict. | `test-issue135-link-verdicts.sh`, including mocked absent, present, unreachable, and malformed archive responses. The Links job also runs tests that enforce the terminal gate. |\n| Restore disk measurement | The historical temporary-file bug had already been repaired on main. Add its regression to measurement preflight. Require preflight success before installation, require fresh output, validate it before replacing tracked data and rendering README, and only publish from main. Distinguish git diff errors from a changed file. Reject non-finite totals or component sizes and an all-zero component set. | `test-issue125-budget-state-survives-tmp-cleanup.sh` and `test-issue135-measure-workflow.sh`. [Manual branch validation](https://github.com/link-foundation/box/actions/runs/45954663314) executes the installer and output pipeline without publication. |\n| Audit remaining workflows, warnings, errors and misleading passes | Inspect the six other named workflow groups and the successful and failing adjacent runs. Retain the security, formatting, file size, docs, Dockerfile, workflow and release gates. Fix the Scripts fixture that could fail on a valid anchor. | [Run and signal disposition](#run-and-signal-disposition), [extracted annotations](github/actions-command-census.tsv), and the PR workflow runs. |\n| Compare all four template trees and adopt applicable practices | Pin all trees, index every workflow, action and CI script, compare their roles and root tools, and map Hive Mind's practices to the Box pipeline. | [Template comparison](templates.md), complete tracked trees and CI file fingerprints in [github](github/). |\n| Report genuinely shared issues | Reproduced wrong HTTP-method recovery in JS, Python and PHP. Reproduced unavailable/missing archive conflation in Python and PHP. Rust's current check already uses GET. | Five [public reports](upstream/reports.txt) with isolated reproduction, workaround, and code suggestions. [Fixture output](verification/). |\n| Leave diagnostics available for the next run | The Links dispatch input enables scanner verbosity and per-request retry diagnostics. Measurement dispatch exposes the existing opt-in diagnostics to the budget wrapper. | Workflow regression assertions. Both dispatch inputs default to false. |\n| Ship one reviewed change with release automation | Use the repository's changeset to trigger an automatic patch after merge. Keep the evidence and regressions in PR 136. | [Changeset](../../../../../../.changeset/ci-verdicts.md), Actions checks for the current PR head, and Git ancestry of main. |\n\n## Timeline and root causes\n\n| UTC date | Evidence and disposition |\n| --- | --- |\n| 2026-09-10 | Measurement run [34455018634](https://github.com/link-foundation/box/actions/runs/34455018634) failed. Lines 649–655 show removal of the wrapper's state after the installer cleans system temp, while 2453–2454 show the propagated exit 1. The installer deliberately removes files inside system temp; the parent wrapper had stored its status and forwarding files there. PR 126 moved state into `RUNNER_TEMP`. The historical artifact had expired by audit time; our earlier [PR 126 evidence](https://github.com/link-foundation/box/tree/main/dev/log/issues/125/pulls/126) preserves the successful measurements. |\n| 2026-10-06 | Links [37466341052](https://github.com/link-foundation/box/actions/runs/37466341052) failed on an HTTP 503 from a healthy GitHub Discussion. This was a temporary response. Commit `2095b5c` added bounded recovery of temporary status codes. |\n| 2026-10-11 | Scripts [38157957100](https://github.com/link-foundation/box/actions/runs/38157957100) failed the valid-anchor fixture at lines 1070–1102. The fixture piped complete program output through `grep -q` with `pipefail`. A match lets grep exit before the producer finishes, so the producer can receive SIGPIPE. A bounded reproduction recorded exit 141 in the verification logs. The committed test now captures output and command status separately before checking the anchor. |\n| 2026-10-13 | Links [38406835991](https://github.com/link-foundation/box/actions/runs/38406835991) identified 30-second timeouts for the Ubuntu package page. Existing commit `d8d7c0c` documents that service in the ignore file. |\n| 2026-10-14 | The release, docs, sizes, scripts, workflows and links runs for `a63b605` succeeded. |\n| 2026-11-10 | Links [42833999978](https://github.com/link-foundation/box/actions/runs/42833999978) was green on the same source subsequently checked by the November failures. This bounds the observation window without establishing when the upstream GitHub repository stopped being public. |\n| 2026-11-17 / 2026-11-24 | Both scheduled Links scans reached the old repository URL and returned 404. Both suggested the archive from 2020-10-11. The repeatable live 404 explains the failed gate. Local fixture tests separately found the latent false-green and diagnostic defects. |\n| 2026-11-27 | Issue 135 was opened and PR 136 linked. The audit reproduced the historical disk regression and link false green, compared the pinned trees, and filed shared defects upstream. |\n\n## Run and signal disposition\n\n| Named run | Recorded result | Disposition |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 45443984715 Links | Failed | Genuine persistent GitHub 404. Correct the authored link. |\n| 45220072505 Security | Passed | CodeQL and secret scanning succeeded. The selected tables and job metadata carry the actual check conclusions. |\n| 38633908376 File sizes | Passed | Size gate and its final status passed. |\n| 38633908390 Build and Release | Passed | Build and publication completed. The raw GH archive replaces the formatted CLI output, which hit the job-log download request limit. |\n| 38633908272 Docs | Passed | Required documentation and final status passed. |\n| 38633908325 Scripts | Passed | Static and regression jobs passed. Adjacent earlier anchor failure repaired by this PR. |\n| 38633908273 Workflows | Passed | Workflow lint/audit and terminal status passed. |\n| 34455018599 Dockerfiles | Passed | Hadolint accepted the Dockerfiles and final status passed. |\n| 34455018634 Measure Disk Space | Failed | False negative for the installer, accurate failure for evidence capture. Existing wrapper repair plus new preflight, freshness and publication checks. |\n\nThe GitHub command census indexes both streamed logs and raw job archives with line numbers. Repeated terminal errors report the same failed dependency. Successful scan notices point to reports; retries identify recovered URLs. Release job traces also contain commands that would emit warnings in other scenarios. A warning string in a step's echoed shell body is not a runner warning. Actual warnings from stripped manpages are expected in the minimal image, and temporary registry retries can succeed without dropping the final publication verification. Prior suppressed-host cases, prototype fixtures and unexplained external failures were kept distinct. Historical CI statuses show that a green build alone could miss the wrapper ordering, report completeness and GET/HEAD defects.\n\n## Design alternatives and prior art\n\n- Changing the case-study reference preserves source attribution and the historical example. Removing it loses detail, and broadly accepting 404 would hide other dead links. The existing Wayback host exemption addresses bot/rate protection. Preserve the timestamped target given by the runner.\n- Lychee remains the scanner and the authority for anchors. Its [CLI](https://lychee.cli.rs/guides/cli/) uses GET by default. [Lychee issue 2297](https://github.com/lycheeverse/lychee/issues/2297) already tracks connect-phase retries; the bounded retry helper works around that gap. Switching to structured JSON could simplify report validation in a future action change. Pinning the existing textual contract keeps the PR's human-readable job summary and both consumers together. PHP and Python's archives illustrate why a single boolean or nullable URL cannot describe lookup availability.\n- GitHub's [job dependency semantics](https://docs.github.com/en/actions/using-jobs/using-jobs-in-a-workflow) already give the needed preflight gate. A fresh output pathname allows the existing validator and renderer to run as-is under their normal entry points. Timestamp heuristics and the committed JSON cannot prove the installer produced a document. The budget wrapper and existing status gate preserve capacity and outcome diagnostics.\n- The existing Box Actions and shell tooling already solve image-specific CI. Replacing the release chain with package workflows would lose native multi-architecture builds and registry validation. Compare interfaces and failure semantics using the role matrix, then reuse matching practices.\n\n## Evidence and reproduction\n\n- [ci-logs](ci-logs/) holds compressed Actions logs. For `.log.gz`, use `gzip -dc`; for `.zip`, use `unzip -l` and `unzip -p ARCHIVE 'MEMBER'`. The adjacent `.error.txt` files document the formatted CLI's download-limit failures before the raw archive fallback.\n- [artifact-metadata](artifact-metadata/) and [job-metadata](job-metadata/) preserve GitHub API details for the cited runs. The historical measurement artifact expired. [Release build records](artifacts/) retain the 56 available OCI archives with [SHA-256 checksums](artifact-metadata/release-artifact-checksums.txt).\n- [github](github/) holds the primary data and the complete tree inventories. [research](research/) contains the pinned Lychee formatter and the prior workflow. [upstream](upstream/) contains submitted text and issue URLs.\n- From the repository root, run `python3 experiments/issue-135/index-evidence.py` to regenerate the census and role index. Run `python3 experiments/issue-135/reproduce-head-get.py . node scripts/ci/recheck-broken-links.mjs` for the bounded network-free loopback reproduction.\n- Run the new offline suites with `bash experiments/test-issue135-link-verdicts.sh` and `bash experiments/test-issue135-measure-workflow.sh`. Each uses mocks or validates narrowly scoped workflow structure. The runner installs the real components in the manual measurement.\n| Links, archive and retry | JS and Rust already have richer archive behavior. Rust's recheck uses GET and report accounting. Use matching semantics in both Box readers. PHP, Python and JS HEAD tests reproduced the false green, and PHP and Python archive tests reproduced the outage ambiguity. File the five reports recorded with the evidence. |\n| Workflow audit, path filtering, terminal status, superseded runs and job budgets | Box uses workflow syntax/lint, Zizmor, checkout-credential checks, path coverage, and per-job budget checks, together with a final aggregate check. JS and Rust additionally auto-rerun selected infrastructure failures. Box classifies failures in its native release, registry, and supersede helpers. A blanket rerun can delay stable failures and duplicate expensive builds. |\n| Tests, examples, language gates and app builds | JS first-gate/example and Rust desktop workflows check the package template's application and architecture contracts. Box checks shipped shell/JS/Python scripts, shell format, Dockerfiles, regression experiments, runtime smoke scenarios, and its real Linux container matrix. Package-specific source, lockfile and runtime matrices target delivered package code. Box provisions several toolchains but has no product package manifest for those managers. |\n| Release plumbing, credentials, state and artifact transport | Templates publish packages and some examples or desktop binaries. Box publishes native AMD64/Arm64 images and consumes digest/manifest, registry credential probes and build-chain artifacts. Changesets drive versions, the actual merge is checked, and per-registry retry helpers classify failures. Retain workflow-specific publication logic and only use archive transport for a demonstrated artifact service problem. |\n| Docs, template self-consistency and file limits | PHP and Python have separate docs gates, and PHP checks multiple template surfaces. Box has required-doc and link checks and a separate file line budget. Historical logs are archived separately from active code so representation does not affect the production gates. |\n| Dependabot, dependencies, secret scanning and security | Python includes a bot-health workflow. All four have security gates, with tools matching their packages. Box scans shell-dependent workflows and source with Zizmor, CodeQL and Secretlint, and validates installed image versions and pull/publish paths. Language package install and audit policies apply to template package lockfiles. Box's dependency surface consists primarily of the base image, tools installed by Dockerfiles, and external actions. A comprehensive OS/image vulnerability scan would be distinct work; current coverage verifies versions, Dockerfiles, and workflow dependencies. |\n| Shell/container-specific infrastructure | Box has distinct jobs for disk reclaim, swap, budget telemetry and component size tracking. The template package workflows lack that system-wide installer. Keep its dedicated workflow, and use ordinary job prerequisites and validated artifacts to eliminate false results. |\n| Development helper scripts and hook tooling | Hooks and automated changeset checks retain the same duties across implementations. Box's shell hook reuses the CI checks. Package release scripts, project scaffold helpers, development examples and build-specific binary tools were kept in their template roles. |\n\n## Hive Mind practices\n\nThe source guidance is [the Hive Mind CI/CD document](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/main/docs/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md). This table records the Box checks and the specific application choices that affect verdicts.\n\n| Practice | Application in Box |\n| --- | --- |\n| 1. Run relevant checks | Workflow path filters cover lint inputs, tested by `check-workflow-path-coverage.mjs`. Release's path classifier determines the affected image tiers. PR validation runs fast tests even when expensive publication is disabled, and a manual or main run can exercise the installer. |\n| 2. File line limits | `file-sizes.yml` invokes `check-file-line-limits.sh` and propagates failures. |\n| 3. Automated formatting | Scripts and local hooks use `run-shfmt.sh` for shipped and test shell. |\n| 4. Static analysis | Scripts check heredocs, awk portability, JavaScript and Python syntax, and ShellCheck. Dockerfiles use Hadolint. Security uses CodeQL where supported. |\n| 5. Fast failures | Release validates inputs before image build jobs. The disk install now requires its fast preflight, including a wrapper cleanup regression. |\n| 6. Changesets | `.changeset/ci-verdicts.md` triggers an automated patch. Changeset scripts validate, coalesce and apply changes before publication. |\n| 7. Check the merge result | `simulate-fresh-merge` runs relevant PR workflows against a fresh merge; use repository-controlled safe checkout behavior. |\n| 8. Local hooks | `.githooks/pre-commit` and `scripts/install-git-hooks.sh` expose the same checks early. |\n| 9. Automated releases | The release orchestrator prepares versions, calls native build workflows, creates multi-arch manifests and validates publication. |\n| 10. Concurrency | Scoped concurrency groups and the supersede helper ensure replaced runs can stop without converting current failures into successes. Measure's slow request and PR validation use separate groups. |\n| 11. Detect secrets | Security uses Secretlint and the Box experiment suite tests masking opt-in credential diagnostics. Existing checkout permission validation remains in place. |\n| 12. Documentation | Dedicated Docs and Links workflows. Link recovery leaves anchors/local files to Lychee and keeps 404 and archived-only live failures red. |\n| 13. Native container architectures | Release tiers use Ubuntu AMD64 and Arm64 runners, publishing combined platform manifests. |\n| 14. Lint workflows | Workflow syntax, Zizmor and explicit job/status/path and permission checks validate workflow behavior. |\n| 15. Audit dependency trees | Existing workflow dependency audits check actions; Box's image dependencies are installed by the platform/Dockerfiles, and the PR version and runtime scenarios verify those contracts. Template-specific npm/Cargo/uv/Composer lockfile audits require a package dependency tree. |\n| 16. Preflight publishing | `preflight` verifies release credentials and relevant registry operations. PR jobs do not require write credentials; disk measurements run on the branch but can only publish from main. |\n| 17. Classify the real failure | Link scan failure differs from unavailability of the scanner or archive service. Disk generation validates fresh files before output publishing. Existing terminal status, supersede and retry classifiers preserve cancellations and originating failure types. |\ntotal 120\ndrwxr-xr-x  2 box box 4096 Nov 27 07:09 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 10 box box 4096 Nov 27 07:08 ..\n-rw-r--r--  1 box box  436 Nov 27 07:00 box-baseline-head-get.log\n-rw-r--r--  1 box box  239 Nov 27 07:00 box-head-get.log\n-rw-r--r--  1 box box  152 Nov 27 07:04 check-checkout-credentials.mjs.log\n-rw-r--r--  1 box box 1150 Nov 27 07:04 check-status-gate-covers-all-jobs.mjs.log\n-rw-r--r--  1 box box   87 Nov 27 07:04 check-timeout-budgets.mjs.log\n-rw-r--r--  1 box box  126 Nov 27 07:04 check-workflow-path-coverage.mjs.log\n-rw-r--r--  1 box box   75 Nov 27 06:58 check-workflow-yaml.sh.log\n-rw-r--r--  1 box box  196 Nov 27 07:04 dead-github-repository.log\n-rw-r--r--  1 box box   98 Nov 27 07:09 fresh-measurement-validation.log\n-rw-r--r--  1 box box   64 Nov 27 07:09 js-archive-urls.log\n-rw-r--r--  1 box box  277 Nov 27 06:53 js-head-get.log\n-rw-r--r--  1 box box   90 Nov 27 07:07 nonfinite-measurement-baseline.log\n-rw-r--r--  1 box box   88 Nov 27 07:09 php-archive-urls.log\n-rw-r--r--  1 box box  110 Nov 27 07:04 php-archive.log\n-rw-r--r--  1 box box  249 Nov 27 06:53 php-head-get.log\n-rw-r--r--  1 box box   89 Nov 27 07:09 python-archive-urls.log\n-rw-r--r--  1 box box  217 Nov 27 06:57 python-archive.log\n-rw-r--r--  1 box box  253 Nov 27 06:53 python-head-get.log\n-rw-r--r--  1 box box  162 Nov 27 06:53 rust-head-get.log\n-rw-r--r--  1 box box 2309 Nov 27 06:58 test-issue115-links-gate.log\n-rw-r--r--  1 box box 2419 Nov 27 06:58 test-issue121-links-recheck.log\n-rw-r--r--  1 box box  288 Nov 27 06:58 test-issue125-budget-state-survives-tmp-cleanup.log\n-rw-r--r--  1 box box  749 Nov 27 06:58 test-issue131-links-recheck.log\n-rw-r--r--  1 box box  441 Nov 27 06:58 test-issue135-link-verdicts.log\n-rw-r--r--  1 box box  244 Nov 27 07:14 test-issue135-measure-workflow.log\n-rw-r--r--  1 box box   26 Nov 27 07:02 valid-anchor-sigpipe.log\n-rw-r--r--  1 box box  295 Nov 27 07:00 wayback-availability.log\n-rw-r--r--  1 box box   11 Nov 27 07:04 wayback-replay.log\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
