/github.com/link-foundation/python-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template\n- https://github.com/link-foundation/php-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template\n\nWe should compare all files, so we don't have more CI/CD errors in the future and reuse all the best practices from these templates.\n\nFollow the CI/CD best practices collected in [https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/main/docs/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/main/docs/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md).\n\nPlease plan and execute everything in this single pull request, you have unlimited time and context, as context auto-compacts and you can continue indefinitely, until it is each and every requirement fully addressed, and everything is totally done.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Context collected by <code>/fix --ci-cd</code></summary>\n\n- **Repository:** [link-foundation/box](https://github.com/link-foundation/box)\n- **Default branch:** `main`\n- **Latest commit:** `a89c079` ([commit](https://github.com/link-foundation/box/commit/a89c0791b282823b772ff71b66169fe6e3efea90)) — 2.10.5: Start the nested Docker daemon in a box resumed from a docker commit snapshot by removing dockerd and containerd pid files left by the previous container. Keep the containerd pid file while containerd is still running so live restore can reuse it.\n- **CI/CD runs found:** 9 (2 not passing)\n\n**Detected languages**\n\n- **Shell** — 40.8%\n- **JavaScript** — 32.1%\n- **Rust** — 8.8%\n- **Python** — 8.4%\n- **HTML** — 5.5%\n- **PHP** — 3.5%\n- **Dockerfile** — 0.9%\n\n**Recommended CI/CD templates**\n\nApply the best practices from these templates, in priority order (most-used language first):\n\n1. **JavaScript / TypeScript** — [link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template](https://github.com/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template) _(detected: JavaScript)_\n2. **Rust** — [link-foundation/rust-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template](https://github.com/link-foundation/rust-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template) _(detected: Rust)_\n3. **Python** — [link-foundation/python-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template](https://github.com/link-foundation/python-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template) _(detected: Python)_\n4. **PHP** — [link-foundation/php-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template](https://github.com/link-foundation/php-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template) _(detected: PHP)_\n\nOther detected languages without a dedicated template: Shell, HTML, Dockerfile.\n\n</details>\nFixes #135\n\n## Findings and changes\n\n- The November scheduled link failures both came from a persistent GitHub 404 in the issue 80 case study. The reference now points to the timestamped Wayback snapshot confirmed by the availability API.\n- Link recovery now matches Lychee's GET, requires complete failure reports, and preserves permanent, local and anchor failures. A scanner execution error and an unavailable Wayback lookup each get their own diagnostic.\n- The historical disk failure came from installer cleanup deleting the observer's temporary files. The existing fix now has a regression in measurement preflight. The main measurement depends on that preflight, validates a fresh JSON file before updating tracked files, and only publishes from main.\n- The Scripts anchor fixture now captures the producer's output before checking it, removing a SIGPIPE race. A changeset triggers the automatic patch release.\n\n## Reproduction and verification\n\n- Run `python3 experiments/issue-135/reproduce-head-get.py . node scripts/ci/recheck-broken-links.mjs`. The loopback endpoint answers HEAD 200 and GET 404. The old helper reports recovery and the new helper keeps the failure.\n- Run `bash experiments/test-issue135-link-verdicts.sh` to check mixed Lychee reports, incomplete reports, request methods, and the archive outage verdict.\n- Run `bash experiments/test-issue125-budget-state-survives-tmp-cleanup.sh` and `bash experiments/test-issue135-measure-workflow.sh` to check the original cleanup regression and the workflow's output and publication gates.\n- The [live disk measurement](https://github.com/link-foundation/box/actions/runs/45954663314) runs the real installer and renderer on the PR branch with publication disabled.\n- The [audit record](https://github.com/link-foundation/box/tree/issue-135-85870cf3b42a/dev/log/issues/135/pulls/136) contains the timeline, line-numbered evidence, compressed Actions logs, complete template trees, the guidance comparison and local checks. GitHub reported the historical measurement artifact as expired. The logs remain in the audit record.\n\n## Shared template findings\n\n- HTTP-method recovery: [JS #322](https://github.com/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/322), [Python #170](https://github.com/link-foundation/python-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/170), [PHP #41](https://github.com/link-foundation/php-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/41).\n- Wayback outcome ambiguity: [Python #171](https://github.com/link-foundation/python-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/171), [PHP #42](https://github.com/link-foundation/php-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/42).\nname: Measure Disk Space and Update README\n\non:\n  push:\n    branches:\n      - main\n    paths:\n      - 'scripts/ubuntu-24-server-install.sh'\n      - 'scripts/measure-disk-space.sh'\n      - 'scripts/update-readme-sizes.sh'\n      - 'Dockerfile'\n      - '.github/workflows/measure-disk-space.yml'\n  # The measurement itself takes ~3 hours and pushes to main, so it cannot run\n  # on a pull request. What CAN run on a pull request is everything that decides\n  # whether the measurement is going to work at all — and it has to, because\n  # this workflow only ever ran after the merge. Run 33972074753 (main, commit\n  # 42be663) is the case in point: `NODE_MAJOR: unbound variable` was\n  # introduced, reviewed and merged without a single job ever executing the\n  # changed script (issue #115).\n  pull_request:\n    types: [opened, synchronize, reopened]\n    paths:\n      - 'scripts/ubuntu-24-server-install.sh'\n      - 'scripts/measure-disk-space.sh'\n      - 'scripts/update-readme-sizes.sh'\n      - 'ubuntu/24.04/common.sh'\n      - 'data/disk-space-measurements.json'\n      - '.github/workflows/measure-disk-space.yml'\n      # The preflight and validation jobs, which are what a pull request can\n      # run here, are the only place these three are executed at all. They are\n      # deliberately absent from the push filter above: editing a validator\n      # should re-run the validation, not spend three hours measuring disk.\n      - 'scripts/ci/extract-quoted-heredoc.sh'\n      - 'scripts/ci/validate-measurements.py'\n      - 'scripts/ci/summarize-measurements.py'\n      - 'scripts/ci/run-with-budget-warning.sh'\n      - 'experiments/test-issue125-budget-state-survives-tmp-cleanup.sh'\n      - 'experiments/test-issue135-measure-workflow.sh'\n  # Allow manual trigger\n  workflow_dispatch:\n    inputs:\n      force_update:\n        description: 'Force update README even if no changes detected'\n        required: false\n        type: boolean\n        default: false\n      verbose:\n        description: 'Trace what the measurement script resolves, generates and hands to the box user (BOX_VERBOSE=1)'\n        required: false\n        type: boolean\n        default: false\n\n# Least-privilege default; the measurement job escalates to `contents: write`\n# for its push. The validation job never needs more than a read.\npermissions:\n  contents: read\n\nenv:\n  # actions/checkout's first act is `git init`, and a git with no configured\n  # `init.defaultBranch` answers it with a thirteen-line advice block - \"Using\n  # 'master' as the name for the initial branch... this default branch name will\n  # change\" - at the top of every job log. 19 checkouts in the runs issue #121\n  # lists printed 247 lines of it, in jobs where nothing was wrong. No step can\n  # fix it, because it is printed before the first step of ours runs; git reads\n  # configuration from the environment too, and the environment is there from\n  # the start. Ported from the js template, which carries the same three lines\n  # with the same reasoning.\n  GIT_CONFIG_COUNT: '1'\n  GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0: ini…nch\n  GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0: main\n\njobs:\n  # Fast pre-merge gate. Nothing here installs anything, so it finishes in\n  # under a minute and can run on every pull request that touches the scripts.\n  validate:\n    name: Validate measurement scripts\n    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n    timeout-minutes: 10\n    concurrency:\n      group: check-${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}-validate\n      cancel-in-progress: true\n    steps:\n      - name: Checkout repository\n        uses: actions/checkout@v6\n        with:\n          persist-credentials: false\n\n      # A pull_request checkout is GitHub's merge preview, computed when the\n      # pull request was last synchronised and never recomputed as main moves.\n      # Merge the base branch first, so this job reports on what merging would\n      # actually produce (issue #115, best practice #7).\n      - name: Simulate a fresh merge with the base branch\n        uses: ./.github/actions/simulate-fresh-merge\n\n      - name: Syntax-check the scripts\n        run: |\n          for f in scripts/measure-disk-space.sh scripts/ubuntu-24-server-install.sh scripts/update-readme-sizes.sh; do\n            echo \"bash -n $f\"\n            bash -n \"$f\"\n          done\n\n      # The generated script is written from a quoted heredoc, so `bash -n` on\n      # the parent says nothing about it. Extract it and check it separately.\n      #\n      # The extraction used to be an inline awk pattern that hardcoded the\n      # spacing of the opener (`cat > /tmp/box-measure.sh <<`). shfmt then\n      # reformatted the script to `cat >/tmp/box-measure.sh <<'EOF_BOX'` and the\n      # pattern matched nothing, failing this job on every push (issue #115,\n      # RC-22). The extraction now matches what bash parses rather than how the\n      # line happens to be formatted, and says which of \"no opener\", \"no\n      # terminator\" and \"empty body\" it hit.\n      - name: Syntax-check the generated box-user script\n        run: |\n          bash scripts/ci/extract-quoted-heredoc.sh \\\n            scripts/measure-disk-space.sh EOF_BOX > /tmp/generated-measure.sh\n          echo \"extracted $(wc -l < /tmp/generated-measure.sh) lines\"\n          bash -n /tmp/generated-measure.sh\n\n      - name: Check for variables leaking out of quoted heredocs\n        run: bash scripts/ci/check-heredoc-vars.sh\n\n      - name: Regression tests for issue #115\n        run: bash experiments/test-issue115-heredoc-unbound-vars.sh\n\n      # Argument handling is the other half of what broke: the documented\n      # no-argument invocation used to abort on `$1: unbound variable`.\n      - name: Regression tests for measurement output and budget state\n        run: |\n          bash experiments/test-issue125-budget-state-survives-tmp-cleanup.sh\n          bash experiments/test-issue135-measure-workflow.sh\n\n      - name: Check the command line interface\n        run: |\n          ./scripts/measure-disk-space.sh --help > /dev/null\n          if ./scripts/measure-disk-space.sh --not-an-option 2>/dev/null; then\n            echo \"::error::an unknown option must be rejected\"; exit 1\n          fi\n\n      # The committed measurements feed the README table; a malformed file\n      # would only be noticed three hours into the next measurement run.\n      - name: Validate the committed measurements\n        run: python3 scripts/ci/validate-measurements.py data/disk-space-measurements.json\n\n  measure-disk-space:\n    name: Measure Component Disk Space\n    # Pull requests stop at `validate`; measuring installs every toolchain on a\n    # bare runner and ends in a push to main.\n    if: github.event_name != 'pull_request'\n    needs: validate\n    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n    # 180 was \"3 hours max for full installation measurement\" - a number nobody\n    # had checked against a run. Every successful run of this job in the\n    # repository's history finished inside 23.3 minutes, the slowest of them in\n    # February (dev/log/issues/121/pulls/122/analysis/); 60 leaves more than\n    # twice that and still bounds a hang at an hour instead of three (issue\n    # #121, docs/CI-TIMEOUT-BUDGETS.md).\n    timeout-minutes: 60\n    # This job commits to main. Cancelling it mid-`git push` is worse than\n    # letting a superseded run finish, so it queues instead of cancelling —\n    # unlike the pre-merge checks above.\n    concurrency:\n      group: measure-disk-space-${{ github.ref }}\n      cancel-in-progress: false\n\n    # pull-requests: write is for the fallback path in\n    # scripts/release/git-push-with-retry.sh only (issue #121).\n    permissions:\n      contents: write\n      pull-requests: write\n\n    env:\n      # Off by default. `workflow_dispatch` can turn it on without editing the\n      # workflow, which is the whole point of having it (issue #115).\n      BOX_VERBOSE: ${{ inputs.verbose && '1' || '0' }}\n\n    steps:\n      - name: Checkout repository\n        uses: actions/checkout@v6\n        with:\n          # Kept, unlike every other checkout here: this job commits the\n          # measured table back to main, so the push needs the credential\n          # checkout leaves in .git/config. Stated rather than left to the\n          # default, so the one job that needs it is the one that says so.\n          persist-credentials: true\n          fetch-depth: 0\n          token: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}\n\n      - name: Free up disk space\n        run: |\n          echo \"=== Initial disk space ===\"\n          df -h /\n\n          echo \"\"\n          echo \"=== Freeing up disk space ===\"\n\n          # Remove large directories that won't affect apt functionality\n          # NOTE: We intentionally do NOT run apt-get remove/autoremove as it breaks\n          # package installation. See docs/case-studies/issue-29 for details.\n          sudo rm -rf /usr/share/dotnet\n          sudo rm -rf /usr/local/lib/android\n          sudo rm -rf /opt/ghc\n          sudo rm -rf /opt/hostedtoolcache\n          sudo rm -rf /usr/local/share/boost\n          sudo rm -rf \"$AGENT_TOOLSDIRECTORY\"\n          # The hosted image ships Homebrew owned by runner. The measurement\n          # installs it as box and must measure a fresh installation.\n          sudo rm -rf /home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew\n\n          # Refresh apt cache to ensure all packages are available\n          source ubuntu/24.04/common.sh\n          apt_update_with_retry\n\n          echo \"\"\n          echo \"=== Disk space after cleanup ===\"\n          df -h /\n\n      - name: Create data directory\n        run: mkdir -p data\n\n      - name: Run disk space measurement\n        id: measure\n        env:\n          BUDGET_VERBOSE: ${{ inputs.verbose && '1' || '0' }}\n        run: |\n          set -o pipefail\n          echo \"=== Starting disk space measurement ===\"\n\n          # Make script executable\n          chmod +x scripts/measure-disk-space.sh\n\ndiff --git a/scripts/measure-disk-space.sh b/scripts/measure-disk-space.sh\nindex 8f743a8..3907906 100755\n--- a/scripts/measure-disk-space.sh\n+++ b/scripts/measure-disk-space.sh\n@@ -491,6 +491,10 @@ JSON_OUTPUT_FILE=\"${1:-/tmp/disk-space-measurements.json}\"\n : \"${NVM_INSTALL_VERSION:?must be passed in by scripts/measure-disk-space.sh}\"\n : \"${JAVA_MAJOR:?must be passed in by scripts/measure-disk-space.sh}\"\n \n+# Git and tool installers must look up configuration under the box account.\n+export XDG_CONFIG_HOME=\"$HOME/.config\"\n+export XDG_CACHE_HOME=\"$HOME/.cache\"\n+\n BOX_VERBOSE=\"${BOX_VERBOSE:-0}\"\n # Trace every command when asked. Off by default: this log is already ~1800\n # lines, and `set -x` over a 40-minute install run is unreadable unless you are\n@@ -551,6 +555,7 @@ with open('$JSON_OUTPUT_FILE', 'w') as f:\n   log_success \"Recorded: $name - ${size_mb}MB\"\n }\n \n+measurement_failed=0\n measure_install() {\n   local name=\"$1\"\n   local category=\"$2\"\n@@ -576,6 +581,7 @@ measure_install() {\n   else\n     log_warning \"Installation of $name failed\"\n     add_measurement \"$name\" \"$category\" 0 0\n+    measurement_failed=1\n   fi\n }\n \n@@ -628,9 +634,9 @@ export NVM_DIR=\"$HOME/.nvm\"\n \n # --- Pyenv + Python ---\n install_pyenv_python() {\n-  curl https://pyenv.run | bash\n   export PYENV_ROOT=\"$HOME/.pyenv\"\n   export PATH=\"$PYENV_ROOT/bin:$PATH\"\n+  curl https://pyenv.run | bash || return\n   eval \"$(pyenv init --path)\"\n   eval \"$(pyenv init -)\"\n \n@@ -759,20 +765,38 @@ install_opam_rocq() {\n     eval \"$(opam env --switch=default 2>/dev/null)\" || true\n     opam repo add rocq-released https://rocq-prover.org/opam/released 2>/dev/null || true\n     opam update 2>/dev/null || true\n-    opam pin add rocq-prover --yes 2>/dev/null || opam install rocq-prover -y 2>/dev/null || opam install coq -y 2>/dev/null || true\n+    # Keep compiler failures visible and bound parallel builds on CI runners.\n+    local OPAMJOBS=\"${OPAMJOBS:-2}\"\n+    export OPAMJOBS\n+    if ! opam pin add rocq-prover --yes && ! opam install rocq-prover -y && ! opam install coq -y; then\n+      log_info \"Trying Ubuntu's Coq package after the opam build failed\"\n+      maybe_sudo apt-get install -y coq || return\n+    fi\n+    if command_exists rocq; then\n+      rocq -v\n+    elif command_exists rocqc; then\n+      rocqc --version\n+    else\n+      coqc --version\n+    fi\n+  else\n+    return 1\n   fi\n }\n measure_install \"Opam + Rocq/Coq\" \"Runtime\" install_opam_rocq\n \n # --- Homebrew ---\n install_homebrew() {\n-  NONINTERACTIVE=1 /bin/bash -c \"$(curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Homebrew/install/HEAD/install.sh)\" || true\n+  local installer\n+  installer=\"$(curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Homebrew/install/HEAD/install.sh)\" || return\n+  PATH=\"/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/bin:$HOME/.linuxbrew/bin:$PATH\" NONINTERACTIVE=1 /bin/bash -c \"$installer\" || return\n \n   if [[ -x /home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/bin/brew ]]; then\n     eval \"$(/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/bin/brew shellenv)\"\n   elif [[ -x \"$HOME/.linuxbrew/bin/brew\" ]]; then\n     eval \"$(\"$HOME/.linuxbrew/bin/brew\" shellenv)\"\n   fi\n+  brew --version\n }\n # Use du-based measurement for Homebrew because the outer script pre-creates\n # /home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew before this runs, making the df-delta near-zero.\n@@ -796,6 +820,7 @@ if install_homebrew; then\n else\n   log_warning \"Installation of Homebrew failed\"\n   add_measurement \"Homebrew\" \"Package Manager\" 0 0\n+  measurement_failed=1\n fi\n \n # Load Homebrew\n@@ -808,10 +833,9 @@ fi\n # --- PHP ---\n install_php() {\n   if command -v brew &>/dev/null; then\n-    brew tap shivammathur/php || true\n     export HOMEBREW_NO_ANALYTICS=1\n     export HOMEBREW_NO_AUTO_UPDATE=1\n-    brew install php || true\n+    brew install php || return\n     # `brew link` prints its \"Warning:\" lines on a *successful* link, so the\n     # output was filtered - but `| grep -v \"Warning\" || true` made grep's status\n     # the pipeline's and then discarded it, so a link that failed was\n@@ -825,7 +849,13 @@ install_php() {\n     else\n       printf '%s\\n' \"$brew_link_out\"\n       log_warning \"brew link --overwrite --force php failed (exit $brew_link_status)\"\n+      return \"$brew_link_status\"\n     fi\n+    local php_prefix\n+    php_prefix=\"$(brew --prefix php)\" || return\n+    \"$php_prefix/bin/php\" --version\n+  else\n+    return 1\n   fi\n }\n measure_install \"PHP (via Homebrew)\" \"Runtime\" install_php\n@@ -913,7 +943,8 @@ install_swift() {\n }\n measure_install \"Swift 6.x\" \"Runtime\" install_swift\n \n-log_success \"Box user measurements complete\"\n+log_info \"Box user measurement attempts complete\"\n+exit \"$measurement_failed\"\n EOF_BOX\n \n chmod +x /tmp/box-measure.sh\n@@ -943,10 +974,11 @@ log_debug \"Generated script: /tmp/box-measure.sh ($(wc -l </tmp/box-measure.sh)\n # versions resolved above are passed explicitly; /tmp/box-measure.sh asserts\n # each one (issue #115). `env` is used rather than a bare VAR=value prefix\n # because sudo's env_reset policy rejects unlisted variables.\n+measurement_status=0\n if [ \"$EUID\" -eq 0 ]; then\n-  su - box -c \"env NODE_MAJOR='$NODE_MAJOR' NVM_INSTALL_VERSION='$NVM_INSTALL_VERSION' JAVA_MAJOR='$JAVA_MAJOR' BOX_VERBOSE='$BOX_VERBOSE' bash /tmp/box-measure.sh '$JSON_TMP_COPY'\"\n+  su - box -c \"env NODE_MAJOR='$NODE_MAJOR' NVM_INSTALL_VERSION='$NVM_INSTALL_VERSION' JAVA_MAJOR='$JAVA_MAJOR' BOX_VERBOSE='$BOX_VERBOSE' bash /tmp/box-measure.sh '$JSON_TMP_COPY'\" || measurement_status=$?\n else\n-  sudo -i -u box env \"NODE_MAJOR=$NODE_MAJOR\" \"NVM_INSTALL_VERSION=$NVM_INSTALL_VERSION\" \"JAVA_MAJOR=$JAVA_MAJOR\" \"BOX_VERBOSE=$BOX_VERBOSE\" bash /tmp/box-measure.sh \"$JSON_TMP_COPY\"\n+  sudo -i -u box env \"NODE_MAJOR=$NODE_MAJOR\" \"NVM_INSTALL_VERSION=$NVM_INSTALL_VERSION\" \"JAVA_MAJOR=$JAVA_MAJOR\" \"BOX_VERBOSE=$BOX_VERBOSE\" bash /tmp/box-measure.sh \"$JSON_TMP_COPY\" || measurement_status=$?\n fi\n \n # Copy the updated measurements back to the original location\n@@ -966,6 +998,11 @@ TOTAL_MB=$(awk \"BEGIN {printf \\\"%.2f\\\", $FINAL_MB - $BASELINE_MB}\")\n \n finalize_json_output \"$TOTAL_MB\"\n \n+if [ \"$measurement_status\" -ne 0 ]; then\n+  log_error \"One or more box-user measurements failed. Partial results saved to: $JSON_OUTPUT_FILE\"\n+  exit \"$measurement_status\"\n+fi\n+\n log_step \"Measurement Complete!\"\n log_success \"Total installation size: ${TOTAL_MB}MB\"\n log_success \"Results saved to: $JSON_OUTPUT_FILE\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
