[2026-11-27T07:39:53.699Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_459","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"dir=dev/log/issues/135/pulls/136/verification; gh api repos/micoud/docker-proxy-acl-alpine --jq '{description,fork,default_branch,created_at,pushed_at,archived,parent:.parent.full_name}' >\\\"\"'$dir/proxy-source-mirror.log\" && gh api repos/micoud/docker-proxy-acl-alpine/commits/0448afc1574007bc27ca6711d3fe854226ec74b5 --jq '\"'{sha,author:.commit.author.name,date:.commit.author.date,html_url}' >>\\\"\"'$dir/proxy-source-mirror.log\" && curl -fsSL -o /dev/null -w '\"'Pinned source replay HTTP %{http_code}\\\\n' 'https://github.com/micoud/docker-proxy-acl-alpine/tree/0448afc1574007bc27ca6711d3fe854226ec74b5' >>\\\"\"'$dir/proxy-source-mirror.log\" && cat \"$dir/proxy-source-mirror.log\"; sed -n '\"'121,143p' docs/case-studies/issue-80/research.md\"","aggregated_output":"{\"archived\":false,\"created_at\":\"2020-07-09T11:32:08Z\",\"default_branch\":\"master\",\"description\":\" A lightweight docker Unix socket proxy which restricts endpoint usage to allowed sections\",\"fork\":false,\"parent\":null,\"pushed_at\":\"2019-07-16T04:52:59Z\"}\n{\"author\":\"Quentin McGaw\",\"date\":\"2019-07-16T04:51:53Z\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/micoud/docker-proxy-acl-alpine/commit/0448afc1574007bc27ca6711d3fe854226ec74b5\",\"sha\":\"0448afc1574007bc27ca6711d3fe854226ec74b5\"}\nPinned source replay HTTP 200\nConclusion: **Docker has no native multi-tenant view of `docker ps`.** Anyone who can reach the socket sees all\ncontainers on that daemon.\n\n### 2b. Socket proxies in front of `docker.sock`\n\n- [`Tecnativa/docker-socket-proxy`](https://github.com/Tecnativa/docker-socket-proxy) — HAProxy with environment-flag\n  ACLs on API endpoints (e.g. `CONTAINERS=1 POST=0`). Endpoint-level only; cannot filter response bodies.\n- [`linuxserver/docker-socket-proxy`](https://github.com/linuxserver/docker-socket-proxy) — fork of the Tecnativa\n  proxy.\n- [`titpetric/docker-proxy-acl`](https://github.com/titpetric/docker-proxy-acl) and\n  [`qdm12/docker-proxy-acl-alpine` (archived)](https://web.archive.org/web/20201011040051/https://github.com/qdm12/docker-proxy-acl-alpine) — minimal allowlist proxies for\n  endpoints (sometimes referred to as \"jpillora-style\" though jpillora's project is no longer the canonical one).\n- [`FoxxMD/docker-proxy-filter`](https://github.com/FoxxMD/docker-proxy-filter) — sits behind a Tecnativa-style proxy\n  and **rewrites** API responses, filtering `/containers/json` results by name and by label, returning 404 for\n  inspect/exec/logs on containers that do not match\n  ([explanatory blog post](https://blog.foxxmd.dev/posts/restricting-socket-proxy-by-container/)). This is the\n  closest off-the-shelf primitive for the requested behaviour.\n- [`DataDog/docker-filter`](https://github.com/DataDog/docker-filter) — older, archived, similar idea (read-only\n  filtering proxy).\n\n### 2c. Authorization plugins\n\nDocker's authz plugin API ([docs](https://docs.docker.com/engine/extend/plugins_authorization/)) lets a daemon defer\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
