[2026-11-27T09:05:15.865Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_736","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'full|Full' docs/CI-TIMEOUT-BUDGETS.md | head -32\nsed -n '404,470p' .github/workflows/pr-tests.yml\"","aggregated_output":"21:   finished `cancelled` while `pr-test / dind-full` inside it had `failure`.\n34:\"`pr-test / full` was cancelled\". Points 2 and 3 need the deadline to belong to\n123:This repository sizes caps *and* budgets per matrix leg — the full box gets 90\n127:timeout-minutes: ${{ matrix.variant == 'full' && 90 || 60 }}\n129:  BUDGET_SECONDS: ${{ matrix.variant == 'full' && 3000 || 1350 }}\n153:| `pr-test-full`           | 43.0    | 90  | 90  | build 3000s, test 600s           | 67%   |\n154:| `pr-test-dind` (full)    | 43.4    | 90  | 90  | chain 3000s, image 300s, test 5m | 67%   |\n157:The two 90-minute caps stay: `full` and `dind-full` build JS, essentials,\n158:eleven language images and the full box on one runner, and at 43 minutes\n178:`build-dind-amd64` is the one cap that went **up**. Its slowest leg, the `full`\n193:`measure-disk-space` carried `timeout-minutes: 180  # 3 hours max for full\n            bash scripts/ci/test-box.sh \"$LANGUAGE\" \"box-$LANGUAGE\"\n\n  # --- Tier 4: full box (integration smoke test, all languages on one VM) ---\n  pr-test-full:\n    name: pr-test / full\n    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n    # Stays at 90: measured at 43.0 minutes, and the budgets below reserve 60\n    # of these 90 for a chain that pages through swap when it exports.\n    timeout-minutes: 90\n    needs: [pr-test-language]\n    if: |\n      !cancelled() &&\n      needs.pr-test-language.result == 'success' &&\n      github.event_name == 'pull_request' &&\n      fromJSON(inputs.changes)['should-build'] == 'true'\n    # The guard below cancels this run when its commit is superseded, which\n    # needs write access to the Actions API (issue #112 follow-up).\n    permissions:\n      contents: read\n      actions: write\n    steps:\n      - name: Checkout repository\n        uses: actions/checkout@v6\n        with:\n          persist-credentials: false\n\n      # A queued matrix job can start long after the run was created, by which\n      # time the pull request may have moved on (issue #112 follow-up). Check\n      # before spending a runner on a commit nobody is waiting for.\n      - name: Stop if a newer commit superseded this run\n        env:\n          GH_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}\n          PR_NUMBER: ${{ github.event.pull_request.number }}\n          PR_HEAD_SHA: ${{ github.event.pull_request.head.sha }}\n        run: |\n          bash scripts/ci/supersede.sh stop-if-superseded\n          # ...and keep watching from inside the job. Cancelling from the\n          # outside needs a free runner, and a superseded run holding every\n          # slot is exactly why there is none.\n          setsid nohup bash scripts/ci/supersede.sh watch \\\n            > \"$RUNNER_TEMP/supersede-watch.log\" 2>&1 < /dev/null &\n\n      # A pull_request checkout is GitHub's merge preview, computed when the\n      # pull request was last synchronised and never recomputed as main moves.\n      # Merge the base branch first, so this job reports on what merging would\n      # actually produce (issue #115, best practice #7).\n      - name: Simulate a fresh merge with the base branch\n        uses: ./.github/actions/simulate-fresh-merge\n\n      - name: Free disk space\n        uses: ./.github/actions/free-disk-space\n        with:\n          # The two full-chain jobs are the only ones that hold every language\n          # image and the full box on one VM at the same time, so they reclaim\n          # more than the others (issue #119 follow-up):\n          #\n          #   tool-cache  /opt/hostedtoolcache is ~8 GB of Python/Node/Go/Ruby\n          #               builds for `actions/setup-*`. Nothing here calls one:\n          #               these jobs run bash and docker, and the Node that\n          #               `actions/checkout` needs lives in the runner's own\n          #               externals directory, not in the tool cache.\n          #   swap        removing it reclaims nothing on this image - there is\n          #               no /mnt filesystem for /mnt/swapfile to be on (see the\n          #               `df -a` in run 34259552358) - while `swapoff -a` still\n          #               takes away every page of swap the kernel had. That is\n          #               the wrong side of the trade for a job whose build was\n          #               last seen being SIGKILLed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
