[2026-11-27T09:28:54.184Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_802","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,200p' /tmp/box135-pr.md; ls dev/log/issues/135/pulls/136/verification/current\"","aggregated_output":"Fixes #135\n\n## Findings and changes\n\n- The November scheduled link failures both came from a persistent GitHub 404 in the issue 80 case study. The reference now points to a verified source mirror pinned to the original author’s commit and the timestamped Wayback snapshot confirmed by the availability API.\n- Link recovery now matches Lychee's GET, requires complete failure reports, and preserves permanent, local and anchor failures. A scanner execution error and an unavailable Wayback lookup each get their own diagnostic.\n- The historical disk failure came from installer cleanup deleting the observer's temporary files. The existing fix now has a regression in measurement preflight. The main measurement depends on that preflight, validates a fresh JSON file before updating tracked files, and only publishes from main. A fresh measurement also exposed false passes for Homebrew, PHP, Rocq/Coq, Swift and Lean. The workflow now starts with a clean Homebrew prefix and preserves partial output when an installer fails. Both quoted-heredoc installers receive the Swift candidates explicitly and install Lean before reporting its version.\n- The Scripts anchor fixture now captures the producer's output before checking it, removing a SIGPIPE race. The swap planning fixture now uses controlled swap and disk readings and passes on runners with zero swap. A changeset triggers the automatic patch release.\n\n## Reproduction and verification\n\n- Run `python3 experiments/issue-135/reproduce-head-get.py . node scripts/ci/recheck-broken-links.mjs`. The loopback endpoint answers HEAD 200 and GET 404. The old helper reports recovery and the new helper keeps the failure.\n- Run `bash experiments/test-issue135-link-verdicts.sh` to check mixed Lychee reports, incomplete reports, request methods, and the archive outage verdict.\n- Run `bash experiments/test-issue125-budget-state-survives-tmp-cleanup.sh` and `bash experiments/test-issue135-measure-workflow.sh` to check the original cleanup regression and the workflow's output and publication gates. The disk regression mocks a failed PHP installation, a Swift archive fallback and an unavailable Swift archive, and Lean toolchain installation.\n- The [first full measurement](https://github.com/link-foundation/box/actions/runs/45954663314) reproduced the false passes. The [corrected measurement](https://github.com/link-foundation/box/actions/runs/45957697870) verified the installed runtimes, validated 27 components totaling 12,869 MB, rendered the README, and skipped publication on the PR branch. The PR includes that verified JSON and the generated README table. The [direct-package rerun](https://github.com/link-foundation/box/actions/runs/45960896164) also passed with the published Rocq package and again measured 12,869 MB across 27 components. The offline regression also checks that all server and image installers reject a missing prover and accept a working fallback.\n- The [Docker PR matrix](https://github.com/link-foundation/box/actions/runs/45961808705) passed all 15 language images, all 14 DinD variants and the full-image smoke test at `3297bf6`, the last commit to change runtime sources.\n- The [audit record](https://github.com/link-foundation/box/tree/issue-135-85870cf3b42a/dev/log/issues/135/pulls/136) contains the timeline, line-numbered evidence, compressed Actions logs, complete template trees, the guidance comparison and local checks. GitHub reported the historical measurement artifact as expired. The logs remain in the audit record.\n\n## Shared template findings\n\n- HTTP-method recovery: [JS #322](https://github.com/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/322), [Python #170](https://github.com/link-foundation/python-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/170), [PHP #41](https://github.com/link-foundation/php-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/41).\n- Wayback outcome ambiguity: [Python #171](https://github.com/link-foundation/python-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/171), [PHP #42](https://github.com/link-foundation/php-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/42).\n- Archive target parsing: [JS #324](https://github.com/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/324), [Python #172](https://github.com/link-foundation/python-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/172), [PHP #43](https://github.com/link-foundation/php-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/43).\n- Homebrew bootstrap diagnostic: [Homebrew install #1175](https://github.com/Homebrew/install/issues/1175).\n15181932306-disk-space-measurement.zip\n45957924236.error.txt\n45957924236.log.gz\n45957924252.error.txt\n45957924252.log.gz\n45957924284.error.txt\n45957924284.log.gz\n45957924311.error.txt\n45957924311.log.gz\n45957924336.error.txt\n45957924336.log.gz\n45957924443.error.txt\n45957924443.log.gz\n45957924619.error.txt\n45957924619.log.gz\n45957956651.error.txt\n45957956651.log.gz\n45959146002.error.txt\n45959146002.log.gz\n45959146558.error.txt\n45959146558.log.gz\n45959146588.error.txt\n45959146588.log.gz\n45959146624.error.txt\n45959146624.log.gz\n45959146625.error.txt\n45959146625.log.gz\n45959146647.error.txt\n45959146647.log.gz\n45959146649.error.txt\n45959146649.log.gz\n45959146667.error.txt\n45959146667.log.gz\n45959146869.error.txt\n45959146869.log.gz\n45960896164-artifacts.json\n45960896164-jobs.json\n45960896164-measure-job.log\n45960896164-measurement.json\n45960896164-measurement.log\n45960896164-rest-jobs.json\n45960896164-validator.log\n45960896164.log\n45960902436.error.txt\n45960902436.log\n45961306001.log.gz\n45961312377.log.gz\n45961312384.log.gz\n45961312408.log.gz\n45961312426.log.gz\n45961312481.log.gz\n45961312503.lo